      <p>The reliable approach is to have your vehicle staged before barricades go up, parked on a side street that won't be blocked, with your chauffeur walking to meet your group rather than trying to drive to you mid-parade. Side streets perpendicular to St. Charles that dead-end away from the route — rather than crossing it — tend to stay reachable longest. Tell your chauffeur your viewing spot in advance so this staging happens automatically.</p>

