      <p>The Uptown route runs along St. Charles Avenue through the Garden District and into downtown, and it's the busiest stretch of the season for both crowds and vehicle restrictions. Crossing St. Charles on foot is manageable between floats at marshaled crossing points; crossing it in a car is not an option once a parade is rolling. If your pickup point is on the opposite side of the avenue from where you're standing, plan to walk to a crossing point rather than expecting a vehicle to come around.</p>

